# Host build artefacts must never be copied into the image.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that actually breaks it: the tree installed on
# the host carries platform-specific binaries and `.bin` shims (node.exe on
# Windows), and `COPY . .` would overwrite the Linux tree that `npm ci`
# just installed. The image then fails at exec time, not build time.
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr

# Secrets never belong in an image layer.
.env
.env.*

*.log
